<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Treaty of San Ildefonso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1800">1800</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Treaty of San Ildefonso was a secret agreement signed on 1 October 1800 by which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. In exchange <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> promised a kingdom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruria">Etruria</a>, for the son-in-law of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Charles IV</a> of Spain. Spain kept administering the colony until 1803, when France, after briefly taking possession, sold Louisiana to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, despite having promised Spain never to cede it to a third power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/third-treaty-of-san-ildefonso.jpg" alt="Third Treaty of San Ildefonso" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Milenioscuro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:French_Louisiana_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
